  "lineage": "Brazilian repente and embolada improvised-poetic-dueling traditions of the northeastern Brazilian sertão (Pernambuco, Paraíba, Ceará, Rio Grande do Norte states). Repente is the canonical extended-improvised-verse form of cantadores (poet-singers) performing in pairs, often using rabeca (Northeastern fiddle) or viola (Brazilian ten-string lute) accompaniment. Embolada is the faster-tempo subform with characteristic mocking-and-humorous-couplet improvisation, typically over a pandeiro frame-drum beat.",
